## Library grep (same name or an obviously equivalent statement)
Same-name search: for each of the 21 targets, `grep -rn -E '^(private )?(theorem|lemma) ([A-Za-z_.]*\.)?<name>\b' TCSlib audits --include=*.lean` outside TCSlib/Cryptography/Candidates/: 0 hits for all 21. Inside Candidates/ each name has exactly its own declaration.
Related public lemmas found by name pattern (statClose_*sample*/reject*/firstHit*, *majority_fails*, *shift*, DDH/ElGamal files):
  TCSlib/Cryptography/NumberTheory/Primality.lean:648:theorem statClose_samplePrime (n T : ℕ) (hn : 2 ≤ n) {d : Fin n → Bool}
  TCSlib/Cryptography/Asymptotic/Sampling.lean:542:theorem statClose_firstHit [DecidableEq α] [Nonempty α] (T : ℕ) {d : α} (hd : E d) :
  TCSlib/Cryptography/Asymptotic/Sampling.lean:741:theorem statClose_rejectionSample (m k T : ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) (hk : m ≤ 2 ^ k) (d : Fin m) :
  TCSlib/Cryptography/Asymptotic/OneWayYao.lean:528:theorem statClose_roundSample (n M k c kk : ℕ) (hM : 0 < M) (hMk : M ≤ 2 ^ kk)
  TCSlib/Cryptography/HardcoreBit/PairwiseIndependence.lean:259:theorem uprob_majority_fails_le [Nonempty Ω] [Fintype ι] {X : ι → Ω → Bool}
  TCSlib/Cryptography/ZeroKnowledge/ThreeColoring/Language.lean:391:theorem statClose_sampleEdgeIdx {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) (T : ℕ) :
  None is equivalent to a target: statClose_rejectionSample and statClose_samplePrime are typed samplers (Fin T → Fin k → Bool); statClose_sampleEdgeIdx has stride Nat.size m and T blocks of Nat.size m coins (sampleBelowL m (Nat.size m) n n reads n-bit blocks); statClose_firstHit is the component the target sketch composes; uprob_majority_fails_le is the Chebyshev step of uprob_majOracle_ne_le. No file outside Candidates mentions DDH or El Gamal (grep -l 'ElGamal|elGamal|DDH': only Candidates.lean, Candidates/DiscreteLog.lean, Candidates/ElGamal.lean).


